-- title:
--   Fricke involution sends Δ(q)/Δ(q^N) to N¹² times its inverse
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Write $\Delta(q) \in \mathbb{Q}((q))$ for `deltaSeries`, the Laurent series $q$ times the power series `dedekindEtaUnitQ` (classically $\prod_{n\ge 1}(1-q^n)^{24}$), and let $u_N = \Delta(q)\cdot\Delta(q^N)^{-1}$ be `modularUnitSeries N`, where $\Delta(q^N)$ is the image of $\Delta(q)$ under $q \mapsto q^N$. Let $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the series $j(q^d)$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $N$, and let $w_N =$ `frickeInvolutionFull N` be the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism of $F_N$ defined as follows: if some $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $F_N$ satisfies $\sigma(j(q^a)) = j(q^b)$ for all nonzero $a, b$ with $ab = N$, then $w_N$ is such a $\sigma$ (which one being unspecified), and otherwise $w_N$ is the identity. Assuming $u_N \in F_N$, the theorem asserts that the Laurent series underlying $w_N$ applied to $u_N$, viewed as an element of $F_N$, is $N^{12} \cdot u_N^{-1}$.
--
--   The series $u_N = (\eta(\tau)/\eta(N\tau))^{24}$ is Ogg's modular unit on $X_0(N)$, and the exchanges $j(q^a) \leftrightarrow j(q^b)$ with $ab = N$ encode the Fricke involution $\tau \mapsto -1/(N\tau)$, under which $\Delta(-1/(N\tau))/\Delta(-1/\tau) = N^{12}\Delta(N\tau)/\Delta(\tau)$; the statement is the level-$N$ form of the prime-level result [`ModularCurve.coe_frickeInvolutionFull_modularUnitSeries`](thm.html#ModularCurve.coe_frickeInvolutionFull_modularUnitSeries). It feeds the analysis of minimal primes and fibres attached to the modular unit in the level-ring machinery and the computation of orders of the Fricke image of the modular unit at specialised places.
-- source:
